# BUG-379: an optional flowing into a plain slot -- `var n: int = m.get(k)` -- passed -c and
# failed in Zig with "expected type 'i64', found '?i64'". Both sides were known to the
# checker; it skipped every non-primitive inferred type. Now a diagnostic that names the
# three unwrap spellings. The nil-check narrowing (test/nil_narrow_tc_test.zbr) and
# `if x as v` captures are honoured by the same pass, so guarded code is not flagged.
def main()
    var m = HashMap(str, int)()
    m.set("k", 2)
    var q: int = m.get("k")
    print(q)
